udy rooms","subtitle":"Sterling C. Evans Library · first through fourth floors","notes":"Reserve this option for two or more people working together; bring a shared plan and use the table, whiteboard, and available monitors.","short_summary":"Collaborative rooms across four Evans Library floors, with rooms sized for groups of up to 14.","evidence_claim":"Evans Library group study rooms are on floors one through four and include tables, chairs, and whiteboards; some first- and second-floor rooms have wall monitors.","source_url":"https://library.tamu.edu/spaces/types/group.php","source_title":"Group Study Rooms | University Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"For collaborative activity by groups of two or more; reservations may be made up to a week ahead for up to four hours per day.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"west-campus-library-group-study-rooms","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"West Campus Library Group Study Rooms","title":"West Campus Library group rooms","subtitle":"West Campus Library · second and third floors","notes":"Coordinate with your group before reserving, then use the room’s table, whiteboard, OAL computer, and—where available—large monitor.","short_summary":"Collaborative rooms on the second and third floors of West Campus Library.","evidence_claim":"West Campus Library group study rooms are on the second and third floors and include tables, chairs, whiteboards, and OAL computers; some have large monitors.","source_url":"https://library.tamu.edu/spaces/types/group.php","source_title":"Group Study Rooms | University Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Group rooms are intended for two or more collaborators. The West Campus policy limits a single reservation to three hours and requires two members to check in.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"graduate-professional-student-zone","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Graduate & Professional Student Zone (GPS)","title":"Graduate & Professional Student Zone","subtitle":"Medical Sciences Library · first floor","notes":"If your degree program has GPS access, use its mix of individual and group rooms, OAL computers, and seating styles for research sessions.","short_summary":"A swipe-access graduate study zone with rooms, computers, and varied seating.","evidence_claim":"The Medical Sciences Library’s GPS Zone has group and individual study rooms, OAL computers, and soft, bar-height, and task seating; study rooms are first-come, first-served.","source_url":"https://library.tamu.edu/spaces/types/graduate.php","source_title":"Graduate Study Spaces | University Libraries","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Swipe access is limited to eligible graduate students in specified degree programs; it is generally 24/7 except on home game days and during the winter holiday.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
